var lunrIndex = [{"id":"changelog","title":"Changelog","body":"All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https:\/\/keepachangelog.com\/en\/1.0.0\/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https:\/\/semver.org\/spec\/v2.0.0.html).\n\n## [0.2.0] - 2026-10-29\n\n### Added\n\n- `directio only ...` (alias `with`) removes every imported task that has none of the given attributes, e.g. `directio only security`. `name=value` matches one value; several attributes keep a task with any of them. Nothing is written to the database; re-import to restore.\n\n### Changed\n\n- `directio do ` now explains why nothing ran instead of always saying \"No fixture definitions found for the referenced IDs.\" It names a matching fixture whose task is marked done (with the document and how to re-run it), a fixture no task uses, a filter that matches no fixture ID, or the IDs that have no fixture class.\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2026-10-20\n\n### Added\n\n- `ImportCommand` now prompts the user to flush the fixture cache directory (`.cache`) if it's not empty, similar to the existing logs directory handling.\n- Created `AKlump\\Directio\\IO\\GetCacheDirectory` to provide a centralized and consistent way to retrieve and initialize the `.cache` directory path.\n- Added an optional argument to `FixturesCommand` (alias `do`) that acts as a fixture ID filter, allowing `directio do check_pages_runner` in addition to `directio do --filter=check_pages_runner`.\n- Created `AKlump\\Directio\\Exception\\AuthenticationRequiredException` for fine-grained authentication failure handling.\n- Integrated `Symfony\\Component\\Stopwatch\\Stopwatch` into `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` to print the total generation time for the MHTML archive.\n- Added an optional cache directory parameter to `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` to speed up repeat calls by caching discovered assets.\n- Created `MHTMLTrait` for generating MHTML archives from web pages and their assets.\n- Added `DrupalReports` fixture to facilitate report archival.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- `WriteDocument` writes a document's bytes unchanged instead of trimming them, so an empty document (e.g. after its last task is cut) can be saved; the leading blank line that trimming used to collapse by accident is now handled explicitly when a task is cut.\n- A completed task with no `redo` is now hidden for good by an explicit rule, rather than by an accident of comparing `date_create('')` to the clock.\n- `redo` is now validated as a `DateInterval` period before `import`, `update`, or `fixtures` write anything, instead of throwing partway through a write.\n- Corrected `syntax.md`: the special attribute is `redo`, not `expires` (the code has read `redo` since 2024-10-30); `redo` only accepts a `DateInterval` period, not a datetime; the opening description now says tasks are demarcated by an HTML element, not HTML comments; and the done-once rule (no `redo` means hidden for good) is now stated.\n- Corrected the `fixtures.md` example, which had no task `id` and so could never actually be imported or mapped by `fixtures`.\n- Fixed a bug in `MHTMLTrait` where incorrect `Content-Type` headers were being captured from redirects, causing assets (like SVGs) to be incorrectly labeled as `text\/html`.\n- Improved image display in MHTML archives by ensuring correct `Content-Type` and charset for all assets.\n- Reduced MHTML filesize by using `quoted-printable` encoding for text-based assets (CSS, JS, SVG) instead of `base64`.\n- Added `Snapshot-Content-Location` header to MHTML archives for better browser compatibility.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Task markup is now a Markdown heading ending in a `{ \u2026 }` attribute block (e.g. `## Permissions {#bump_perms redo=P1M}`), not a `\u2026` element. Run `directio convert ` on every existing document \u2014 the source documents and the imported copies under `.directio\/imported\/` \u2014 to rewrite them onto the new syntax in place; `import`, `update`, and `fixtures` refuse a document still on the old markup and say so.\n- `AbstractFixture::shouldRun()` now automatically returns `true` (skipping the confirmation prompt) if a `filter` option is used in the command input.\n- `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` now validates the main response and throws a `FixtureException` if it detects a 403 Access Denied or an unauthorized redirect to a login page (common when a session cookie is missing or expired).\n- Refined `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` to output a single consolidated message: \"Downloaded {url} to {path} in {time}ms\".\n- Removed redundant \"Downloaded\" message from `DrupalReports` fixture.\n- Refined `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` to make `Stopwatch` usage conditional on the class existing and simplified output to show only total generation time.\n- Added a Symfony progress bar to `MHTMLTrait::downloadAsMhtml` to track asset download progress.\n- `MHTMLTrait` now ensures all relative URLs in the HTML content are made absolute, including those in attributes (href, src, etc.) and CSS `url()` references.\n- Refactored `ImportCommand`, `FixturesCommand`, `UpdateCommand`, and `InitializeCommand` to use `SymfonyStyle` for consistent I\/O.\n- Replaced manual `ConfirmationQuestion` usage with `$this->io()->confirm()` across all commands.\n- `ImportCommand` now skips the overwrite prompt when importing files (fixtures, documents, options) if the source and target contents are identical.\n- Updated `ImportCommand` output to indicate when a file is skipped due to identical contents.\n- Updated `ImportCommand`, `FixturesCommand`, `UpdateCommand`, and `InitializeCommand` with the `AsCommand` attribute to resolve Symfony 6.1 deprecations.\n- Refined the final summary message of `ImportCommand` to accurately reflect the number of newly imported versus identical skipped items."},{"id":"completion","title":"Completing Tasks","body":"Given the following task markup:\n\n```markdown\n## Making Dessert {#dessert}\n\n- Measure the eggs and sugar into a bowl\n- Whip for 5 minutes until incorporated\n- Continue mixing the cookies...\n```\n\nTo mark this complete you do two things:\n\n1. Add the completion flag to the heading's `{ \u2026 }` block.\n2. Run the `update` command.\n\n## Completion Markup\n\nAny of the following can be used to indicate completion of a task.\n\n```markdown\n## Making Dessert {#dessert complete}\n## Making Dessert {#dessert done}\n## Making Dessert {x #dessert}\n```"},{"id":"readme","title":"Directio","body":"> Directio is a tool to track tasks over time.\n\nProjects require regular updates. There can be lots of steps to remember, so we write a list of tasks. And then we follow the list each time we do an update. Just to be sure we miss nothing.\n\nAt the start of each update, one makes a duplicate of the tasklist, e.g. _today.md_. Scanning through _today.md_ one notices that some of the tasks have already been done, and are by nature non-recurring. Others recur, but sometimes at different intervals. It's tedius to have to follow along, when not all of the tasks apply to this moment. What if the duplicate somehow KNEW what didn't need to be done today, i.e., what was already completed, or what doesn't need to be done quite yet. What if those tasks were removed from the working file? **Hello Directio.**\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Tasklist File Setup\n\n1. Locate your tasklist file(s) outside of your project, this assumes you want the same tasklist for multiple projects.\n2. Create at least one tasklist, e.g. _\/foo\/bar\/document.md_\n3. Add [Directio syntax](@syntax) to that document.\n\n### Project Usage\n\n1. In the shell, cd to your project root.\n2. `.\/vendor\/bin\/directio import \/foo\/bar\/document.md`\n3. Answer that you want to initialize your project.\n4. Open the created document and mark each task complete.\n5. Use `.\/vendor\/bin\/directio update` to flush the completed tasks from the file.\n\n### Next Time\n\n1. In the shell, cd to your project root.\n2. `.\/vendor\/bin\/directio import \/foo\/bar\/document.md`\n3. Open the created document and notice all completed tasks have been removed.\n4. Continue as before marking complete and updating.\n\n## Documentation\n\n&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n[Read the online documentation](https:\/\/aklump.github.io\/directio\/pages\/general\/readme.html) &rarr;"},{"id":"syntax","title":"Directio Syntax","body":"Each Directio _task_ is a Markdown heading whose last token is a `{ \u2026 }` attribute block, like so:\n\n```markdown\n## Foo Task {#foo}\n...\n```\n\nA task's body runs from its heading down to the next heading of the same or a higher level, or to the end of the document \u2014 there is no closing tag to match. Both [ATX](https:\/\/spec.commonmark.org\/0.31.2\/#atx-headings) (`#` through `######`) and [setext](https:\/\/spec.commonmark.org\/0.31.2\/#setext-headings) (a line of text underlined with `===` or `---`) headings are recognized. A heading found inside a fenced code block (fenced by ```` ``` ```` or `~~~`) is never a task.\n\nA completed task is represented by one slight change. (Look familiar?, i.e., [Markdown task lists](https:\/\/www.markdownguide.org\/extended-syntax\/#task-lists))\n\n```markdown\n## Foo Task {x #foo}\n```\n\n## Alternate Syntax\n\nInstead of `x` you can use boolean attributes (`done`, `complete`) like this:\n\n```markdown\n## Foo Task {done #foo}\n```\n\n```markdown\n## Foo Task {complete #foo}\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n* The `{ \u2026 }` block must be the last token on the heading line.\n* Every task must carry an `id`, either as `#value` shorthand or as `id=value` \/ `id=\"value\"`.\n* Items inside the block are whitespace-separated. Each one is `#name` (shorthand for `id=name`), `name=value`, `name=\"quoted value\"`, or a bare `name` flag.\n* An unquoted value may not contain whitespace, `\"`, `{`, or `}`; wrap it in double quotes (`name=\"quoted value\"`) when it needs to. There is no escape for `\"` itself, so a value can never contain one.\n* Item order is of no significance. If a key appears twice, the later one wins.\n* Tasks may not nest \u2014 a task's body may not contain another task's heading.\n\n## Special Attributes\n\n| Meaning             | Attributes              | Notes                                          | Example               |\n|----------------------|--------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n| task identification  | `id`, `name`             | Must be unique within an initialized project.    | `#foo`, `id=foo`       |\n| Redo after a period  | `redo`                   | A `DateInterval` period.                        | `redo=P1M`, `redo=P1D` |\n| Completed            | `done`, `complete`, `x`  |                                                   | `done`                 |\n| Incompleted          |                          | Tasks are assumed incomplete.                    |                        |\n\nA completed task with no `redo` is hidden for good. A completed task with a `redo` period is hidden until that period has passed since completion.\n\n## Converting Older Documents\n\nDocuments written in the retired `\u2026` element markup can be rewritten onto this syntax in place:\n\n```bash\n.\/directio convert \/foo\/bar\/document.md\n```\n\n`directio convert` prints a summary and asks to confirm before overwriting the file. It preserves every task's `id` and other attributes, so SQLite state recorded under the old syntax still applies afterward.\n\nUnder the new syntax a task's body runs to the next heading at its level or higher, where the old close tag could end it anywhere. Wherever that would change what `update` later removes, the converter refuses and lists the lines rather than guessing: content after a close tag before such a heading, a task with no heading of its own whose body has a level-1 heading, or a task whose heading is deeper than the task before it. Fix those spots in the source and run it again.\n\nConvert the imported copies too \u2014 every document under `.directio\/imported\/` \u2014 or `update` and `fixtures` will refuse them until you do."},{"id":"fixtures","title":"Fixtures","body":"Fixtures allow you to run automated setup or teardown logic as part of your task workflow.\n\n## Autoloading\n\nFixture classes are provided via `autoload` in `.directio\/composer.json`. They must be in the `AKlump\\Directio\\Fixture` namespace.\n\nThe default directory is `.directio\/src\/Fixture\/`. To register additional directories such as `..\/src\/Directio\/Fixture\/`, add to the array as shown below.  **After any changes be sure to run `composer dump-autoload`.**\n\n**File: `composer.json`**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"autoload\": {\n    \"psr-4\": {\n      \"AKlump\\\\Directio\\\\Fixture\\\\\": [\n        \".\/src\/Fixture\/\",\n        \"..\/src\/Directio\/Fixture\/\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe default setup is installed with `directio init`.\n\n## When a Fixture Fails\n\n1. Throw an instance of `AKlump\\Directio\\Fixture\\FixtureException`\n2. It is not necessary to use `$this->io()` to output the exception message, that is automatic.\n\n## Example Class\n\n**File:** `MyFixture.php`\n\n```php"},{"id":"installation","title":"Installation","body":"## Install with Composer\n\n1. Installation requires explicit repositories:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer config repositories.9024aba2baa64b08169c0ca94a832bc7 composer https:\/\/packages.intheloftstudios.com\n   composer config repositories.619ded761a01c386b8878bc732c4cc2a github https:\/\/github.com\/aklump\/directio\n   ```\n\n2. Require the latest stable version:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer require --dev aklump\/directio:^0.1\n   ```\n3. ... or require the dev channel:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer config minimum-stability dev\n   composer require --dev aklump\/directio:@dev\n   ```\n\n## Sandbox Install with Composer\n\nA sandboxed installation separates this project, its dependencies, and even the PHP version from your main application.  In a team environment is allows one member to use a package independently. The project is installed in an isolated, hidden subdirectory in the root directory. This is particularly useful if you have conflicts with your application's dependencies or if you need to use a different PHP version, or you don't want to commit the package to the repo. It functions similarly to [asdf](https:\/\/asdf-vm.com\/) shims, providing a project-specific environment for the tool.\n\n### Install in your Project\n\n1. Create the isolated directory (the sandbox):\n\n   ```shell\n   mkdir -p .directio\n   cd .directio\n   composer init -n --name=sandboxed\/directio\n   composer config version dev-main\n   echo \"vendor\/\" > .gitignore\n   touch README.md\n   echo \"Learn more: https:\/\/github.com\/aklump\/directio\\n\" >> README.md\n   echo \"Execute with: .directio\/vendor\/bin\/directio\\n\" >> README.md\n   ```\n\n1. Installation requires explicit repositories:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer config repositories.9024aba2baa64b08169c0ca94a832bc7 composer https:\/\/packages.intheloftstudios.com\n   composer config repositories.619ded761a01c386b8878bc732c4cc2a github https:\/\/github.com\/aklump\/directio\n   ```\n\n2. Require the latest stable version:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer require --dev aklump\/directio:^0.1\n   ```\n3. ... or require the dev channel:\n\n   ```shell\n   composer config minimum-stability dev\n   composer require --dev aklump\/directio:@dev\n   ```\n\n### Optional: Create the Shim Script\n\nTo override a global binary, or to get around having to call the full path to your sandboxed binary, you can create a shim script. That allows you to call `directio` from anywhere in your project.\n\n1. Create `bin\/shim-composer.sh` in the root of you application from . If you have already done so for another sandboxed package, you can skip this step and reuse that existing script.\n\n   ```shell\n   mkdir -p bin\n   touch bin\/shim-composer.sh\n   chmod u+x bin\/shim-composer.sh\n   ```\n\n#### How it Works\n\nShimming redirects shell commands to the sandboxed version by prepending the sandbox's `bin` directory to your `$PATH`.\n\n```shell\n$ which directio\n\/Users\/aklump\/Code\/Packages\/cli\/directio\/app\/directio\n$ . bin\/shim-composer.sh directio\n\ud83d\ude0e directio shimmed to \/Users\/aklump\/temp\/php81\/.directio\/vendor\/bin\/directio\n$ echo $PATH\n\/Users\/aklump\/temp\/php81\/.directio\/vendor\/bin:\/Applicati...\n$ which directio\n\/Users\/aklump\/temp\/php81\/.directio\/vendor\/bin\/directio\n```\n\n### Sandbox Usage\n\n1. At the start of a new terminal window call the shim script: `. bin\/shim-composer.sh directio`. **Note**: This change lasts only for the current terminal session.\n2. Now simply call `directio` and it will point to `.directio\/vendor\/bin\/directio`\n\n### Sandbox Updates\n\nUpdating your sandboxed installation requires an extra step beyond your main app `composer update`.\n\n```shell\ncd .directio && composer update\n```"},{"id":"only","title":"Keeping Only Some Tasks","body":"Give tasks any attribute you like to group them, e.g. `security`:\n\n```markdown\n## Pre config changes {#pre_config_changes redo=P1D security}\n## Bump dependencies {#bump}\n## Audit permissions {#audit security=high}\n```\n\nThen, in an imported project, keep only that group:\n\n```bash\n.\/vendor\/bin\/directio only security\n```\n\nEvery task in `.directio\/imported\/` that lacks the attribute is removed; `bump` above goes, the other two stay. `with` is an alias: `directio with security`.\n\n* `name` matches a task that has the attribute with any value, or as a bare flag.\n* `name=value` matches only that value, e.g. `directio only security=high`.\n* Several attributes keep a task that has any of them: `directio only security perf`.\n\nNothing is recorded in the database, so removed tasks are not marked done and come back the next time you import the source document. The command lists what it will remove and asks before writing; `-n` skips the question.\n\nIt changes nothing when no task matches, so a typo can't empty your documents. It warns before removing a task that is marked done but not yet saved by `update`, since that completion would be lost."},{"id":"phpstorm","title":"PHP Storm","body":"1. Settings > Editor > Code Style > Markdown\n2. Set _Keep maximum blank lines Around block elements_ to `0`\n3. Set _Minimum blank lines Around block elements_ to `0`"}]